{"id":"st2063","designation":"ST 2063","title":"Stereoscopic 3D Full Resolution Contribution Link Based on MPEG-2 TS","state":"active","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2063/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2063/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This document specifies how a stereoscopic 3D High Definition (“HDTV”) video contribution system based on the MPEG-2 Transport Stream (TS) performs coding, multiplexing, and decoding. It defines constraints for the input image pair, the bitstream, the multiplexing, timing synchronization, use of a single PCR PID, and signaling, as well as for the video coding and decoder behavior. This document is codec agnostic (i.e., any codec for which there are defined methods for transport via MPEG-2 TS is permitted). The input image pair needs to have the same image structure (horizontal and vertical pixel count, scanning system, colorimetry, and frame rate) and be coincident in time.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Definitions and Acronyms","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 Definitions","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"4.2 Acronyms from MPEG-2 Systems (ISO/IEC 13818-1)","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 MPEG-2 Transport Stream Constraints","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Eye Identification Descriptor","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"Video Coding Constraints","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 PES Alignment","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 PCR PID","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Encoder Constraints","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 Visual Fidelity (Informative)","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"7 Decoder Constraints","page":6}],"definitions":[],"keywords":[{"term":"Video Compression","zh":"视频压缩","abbr":"","category":"tv","source":"curated"},{"term":"Chromaticity","zh":"色度","abbr":"","category":"measurement","source":"curated"},{"term":"MPEG",